  "question": {
    "text": "The locus of the middle points of the chords of the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;which subtend an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;at the centre of the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>, is a circle of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
